# ADR-0020 fast/slow-lane scheduling-state split. The three mutable cadence
# columns move off source_config into one row per (source_config, lane), so a
# repair-crawl failure can no longer reset the heartbeat lane's earned interval
# or impose its back-off window (and the reverse).
#
# Operation order is load-bearing in BOTH directions, which is why the generated
# ordering (removals first) was flipped: forward, the lane rows are backfilled
# while the old columns still exist; backward, RemoveField's reverse re-adds the
# columns before the RunPython reverse repopulates them. The AlterField ahead of
# the removal exists only to give current_interval_s a default in migration
# state — without one, the reverse ADD COLUMN of a NOT NULL column against a
# non-empty source_config table fails.
